Package: com.andi.pi-coding-agent
Name: Pi Coding Agent
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64
Maintainer: andi <tafilajandi@gmail.com>
Author: Earendil Works (upstream) / iOS port by andi
Section: Development
Priority: optional
Depends: zsh, bash, python3, ldid, curl, tar, coreutils, ripgrep, fd, uikittools, firmware (>= 15.0)
Recommends: git
Icon: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/@REPO@/main/assets/icon.png
Depiction: https://@PAGES@/depiction.html
Tag: role::developer
Description: Pi, the open-source agent harness, patched for iOS
 Packages Pi @PI_VERSION@.
 .
 Pi is an open-source coding agent that talks to any model provider you have an
 API key for -- Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, Groq, OpenRouter, a local llama.cpp
 and around twenty more. Credentials live in ~/.pi/agent/auth.json or in the
 usual environment variables, so signing in is one file and no keychain.
 .
 Nothing else to install: no Node.js, no npm, no JavaScript runtime. Upstream's
 standalone build is Bun-compiled and self-contained, and this package patches
 it to run on iOS -- Mach-O platform to iOS, a small shim linked in for the
 libSystem symbols iOS lacks, and the macOS framework dlopen paths rewritten.
 .
 The shim also makes JavaScriptCore's JIT work, which iOS otherwise refuses: it
 has no MAP_JIT and will not execute a page that is currently writable, so the
 shim flips the JIT pool between writable and executable with mprotect.
 .
 The 75 MB binary is NOT redistributed here. On install this package downloads
 the official darwin-arm64 tarball from GitHub releases, verifies it against the
 checksum recorded when the package was built, patches and signs it on device,
 and runs it once before installing it. Takes a few seconds and needs a network
 connection.
